%description:

The interference floor a background cell imposes, against the closed form.

A background cell is the modern replacement for an external cell: a base
station with background UEs and a scheduler, but no real protocol stack. What
reaches a real UE from one is a single term, and it is computable -- so this
grades it rather than recording it.

Worth having separately from InterferenceDelta, which covers the same
arithmetic for a real neighbouring cell, because the background path is not
the same code and does not use the same physics. computeExtCellPathLoss
always applies the TR 36.814 formulas whatever propagation study the model
itself is configured with, and it passes the plain distance between the two
nodes as both the three-dimensional and the two-dimensional one. Neither is
obvious from the outside, and a refactoring that unified the two paths would
change the answer without changing anything a fingerprint could attribute.

The scenario is one real cell, one background cell and a UE between them,
with every random ingredient switched off, so both the wanted signal and the
background cell's contribution are sums of configured constants and one path
loss -- from two different studies:

    S = txPower   - PL_38901(d_serving) + Gtx + Grx - cableLoss
    I = bgTxPower - PL_36814(d_bgCell)  + Gtx + Grx - cableLoss
    N = thermalNoise + noiseFigure

As in InterferenceDelta, the background scheduler does not occupy every band
in every TTI and the model counts only the bands it did, so the reported SINR
spans two predictable endpoints: the maximum is the interference-free budget,
from the TTIs in which the background cell was idle, and the minimum is the
fully-loaded one. Both are asserted, which makes the check independent of how
the background load happened to fall.

enableExtCellLos is switched off, so the background link is NLOS by
configuration rather than by borrowing the serving link's LOS state -- which
is what computeExtCellPathLoss does otherwise, and which would make the
expected value depend on a draw belonging to a different link.

%extraargs: -c BackgroundCellFloor

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config BackgroundCellFloor]
output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.SingleCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 5s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
seed-set = 0
**.vector-recording = false
**.measuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max

**.bgCellInterference = ${bgi = true, false}
**.downlinkInterference = false
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

*.gnb.mobility.initialX = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.numUe = 1
*.ue[0].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[0].nrServingNodeId = 1
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 400m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 300m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

**.scenario = "URBAN_MICROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 25m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false
**.enableExtCellLos = false

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
**.numBands = 6
**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm
**.antennGainEnB = 18dBi
**.antennaGainUe = 0dBi
**.cableLoss = 2dB
**.thermalNoise = -104.5dBm
**.ueNoiseFigure = 7dBm

############ one background cell, heavily loaded ############
*.numBgCells = 1
*.bgCell[0].mobility.initialX = 900m
*.bgCell[0].mobility.initialY = 300m
*.bgCell[0].mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.bgCell[0].bgScheduler.isNr = true
*.bgCell[0].bgScheduler.txPower = 40dBm
*.bgCell[0].bgScheduler.txDirection = "OMNI"
*.bgCell[0].bgScheduler.numBands = 6
*.bgCell[0].bgTrafficGenerator.numBgUes = 10
*.bgCell[0].bgTrafficGenerator.bgUE[*].mobility.initialX = uniform(800m,1000m)
*.bgCell[0].bgTrafficGenerator.bgUE[*].mobility.initialY = uniform(200m,400m)
*.bgCell[0].bgTrafficGenerator.bgUE[*].generator.typename = "TrafficGeneratorCbr"
*.bgCell[0].bgTrafficGenerator.bgUE[*].generator.startTimeDl = uniform(0s,0.05s)
*.bgCell[0].bgTrafficGenerator.bgUE[*].generator.packetSizeDl = 1000B
*.bgCell[0].bgTrafficGenerator.bgUE[*].generator.periodDl = 0.001s

*.ue[*].numApps = 1
*.server.numApps = 1
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[*].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue[0]"
*.server.app[0].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].localPort = 3088
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 40B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.02s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=6 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
